From 1ffcb53fe65af072ab5d441a5679d49dec66b0e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: wire concrete Merklix peer handling and transaction
 relay

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics. The candidate repair below
changes this boundary and requires new validation evidence.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Fast-path single-input CheckRegularTransaction duplicate-input checks,
coalesce BlockUndo disk writes, and optimize bulk mempool clear.

Original-Commit: a4ea86865414bbf4f98512bbd4460e2a42897acc
Original-Patch: ecash/020
Split-Concern: relay

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.
Candidate-purpose-redistribution: Place high-bandwidth/batched RPC relay with concrete peer relay methods.

Candidate-Repair: Reconcile already-owned peer-handler dispatch and declarations; retain one dispatch with block-availability bookkeeping and lazy recent-block transaction lookup. Supply batch relay interfaces with existing per-transaction semantics here; retain later peer-lock coalescing in its optimization owner. Move unused incoming ProcessSingleTx/ProcessTxBatch definitions to their actual first consumer49. Exercise real forced high-bandwidth SHORTTX in the existing signed atomic-batch functional fixture.
